# gui/manual.html is BUILT by docs/manual/build.py and served at /manual — and
# it is TRACKED, deliberately, from v2.2 on. It is a release deliverable under
# the docs policy, so a fresh clone and the DMG must both have one; while it
# was ignored, each showed "No manual built yet". packaging/build.py also
# rebuilds it at package time, so the shipped copy is never older than its
# sources. Regenerate and commit it as part of cutting a release.

# docs/manual/build.py also writes a DATED copy beside the sources. It is
# byte-identical to gui/manual.html (which IS tracked), so tracking it too
# would add a fresh 0.55 MB duplicate on every build. The served copy is the
# deliverable; this one is a local convenience.
docs/manual/MANUAL-*.html
